I've written the session plan: two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The command was written with || true for this case, so the files are on disk but not committed.

Task 1: Part of #1111 (product, self-driven). Shell verbs that take no flags will refuse an unknown dash-led word with exit 2 and a did-you-mean, instead of ignoring it. The assessment traced most of #1111's open rows to one function, dispatch_sub::positional_after_verb. It drops every --led word without checking KNOWN_FLAGS, which is why init --froce exits 0 and writes YOYO.md. The task:
• runs its probe over KNOWN_SUBCOMMANDS rather than a typed list of verbs;
• keeps known global flags, and their values, working after a verb;
• puts the tests in a tests/ file, because of the size cap;
• ends with a #1111 comment that opens with "Scope: still open = …" and lists what's left.

Task 2: Fixes #1113 (product, the backlog-drain slot, since 19 issues are open). With the fix, early flag scans skip the word after a flag that takes a value, so yoyo -p --help sends --help as the prompt instead of printing help. The change lives in one place, cli_config::has_option, and the help/version check in dispatch_sub goes through it. Before changing option_args, the task checks who calls it, because parse_args_with_config needs those values. Tests are a table plus one run of the real binary.

